{"id": "Def8WFxEcvB", "title": "Video by kallawaymarketing", "description": "This is the most important hook framework you’ll ever learn.\n\nComment LAUNCH to join the waitlist for my 4 week live content growth program.\n\nEvery video technically has 3 hooks:\n* What you write on screen\n* What you say outloud\n* What you show visually\n\nWhen all 3 of those hooks are aligned, the viewer’s understanding goes way up and the retention metrics are much higher.\n\nBut when the 3 hooks don’t align, the viewer gets confused and usually scrolls away.\n\nIt sounds simple but hook alignment is a major issue in most of the bad videos I review.\n\nNow the best way to improve at your hook alignment is to run the Sound Off and Eyes Closed tests.\n\nWatch the video without sound first and guess what the video is about based on what you see in the visual and text hook.\n\nThen, listen back to the video with your eyes closed and see if what you say matches up.\n\nIf it’s misaligned, you’ve got a hook alignment problem that you need to fix before you post.\n\nIf you want to learn how to build better hooks that actually hold attention, I’m running a 4 week content growth program that goes through my entire content system and workflow.\n\nIt covers everything you need to know about hooks, as well as storytelling, ideation, and AI systems.\n\nComment “Launch” and I’ll add you to the waitlist.\n\nFollow @kallawaymarketing to learn how to grow faster on social media\n \n#marketing #socialmedia #contentcreator #contentstrategy #video", "channel": "kallawaymarketing", "uploader_id": "67218622229", "uploader": "Kallaway", "timestamp": 1792033223, "like_count": 671, "comment_count": 116, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https:/